# The input from which requirements.lock.txt (CPU) and requirements.lock.cu130.txt
# (GPU) are generated. It is NOT installed directly and NOT a lock.
#
# Why it exists (and is not requirements.txt): the AIM backbone is the pinned
# upstream under third_party/ml-aim, imported not copied, so this port's own files
# import only torch, torchvision, numpy and PyYAML (those are requirements.txt).
# But the environment the pinned upstream needs is larger -- ml-aim's model module
# imports huggingface_hub (PyTorchModelHubMixin) -- and the lock must be a closure
# over that whole environment.
#
# Regenerate both locks (from the repository root), as for 36_franca:
#   uv pip compile methods/30_aim/requirements.lock.in --constraint <cpu pins>
#       --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
#       --extra-index-url https://pypi.org/simple --index-strategy unsafe-best-match
#       --python-version 3.12 --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28
#       --generate-hashes --no-annotate --no-header ; then bin/build-lock.py.
torch
torchvision
numpy
PyYAML
huggingface_hub
